   08, 2016},
Abstract = {Over the past decades, we have witnessed changes into how individual's
   pay. In particular, there has been a drop in the use of cash as payment
   instrument both in terms of value and frequency. Consequently, the
   amount of outstanding cash is shrinking. For instance, in Sweden the
   level of cash is around 1.5\% of Gross Domestic Product. This might be a
   tipping point for when cash is of practical use. In the paper, we
   present a research model that explores when merchants will stop
   accepting cash.},
