Title = {The Innovations to Improve the Digital Banking Performance in Romania},
Booktitle = {MULTIDIMENSIONAL EDUCATION \& PROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT. ETHICAL VALUES},
Year = {2016},
Pages = {155-161},
Note = {7th LUMEN International Scientific Conference on Multidimensional
   Education and Professional Development. Ethical Values (MEPDEV),
   Targoviste, ROMANIA, NOV 12-14, 2015},
Organization = {LUMEN},
Abstract = {The banking institutions perceive the impact of the New Information and
   Communication Technology (NICT) differently, yet most of them view it as
   deep and fast, so that 2/3 of them believe that NICT solutions can
   contribute to a better rationalization of the logistics operations and
   even a considerable simplification of the chain supply management. 70\%
   of the companies indicated the capacity of NICT of contributing to a
   profound change in the duties undertaken, which led to an acute need of
   training their employees in this area. The consumer's involvement level
   (high/medium/low) differs depending on how the product meets his
   specific needs. The transition from conventional to electronic payments
   system was favoured primarily by the significant increase in the
   activities developed by the payment systems and then by the need to
   fluidize cashless payments and meet the demands of consumers who ask for
   payments from sister institutions, at efficient and low costs.
   Nowadays, a credit card is a payment instrument applied universally,
   accepted in all countries to provide a wide variety of transactions such
   as purchases of goods and services sold by licensed traders or obtaining
   cash. In Romania, the public can choose between several types of cards
   offered by banks or specialized groups and, furthermore, the current
   trend is to offer financial products by customer classes (based on
   revenue) and/or facilities.
   This report aims an analysis of the development of the Romanian card
   market, especially after the last financial crisis and the banking
   digital instruments proposed by the banks of Romania to attract the
   potential customers. Our work aims also the marketing strategies
   implemented by the Romanian banks focus to growth of digital banking on
   the Romanian market because cash remains still the main payment method
   in Romania.},
