   MALAYSIA, JUL 23, 2022},
Organization = {Universiti Teknologi Mara},
Abstract = {A medical clinic is one of the important healthcare infrastructures that
   provides outpatient services. Oftentimes, a clinic is overcrowded during
   peak times. This causes a problem since clinics tend to have a limited
   number of staff, which is even more problematic during a pandemic. Based
   on the preliminary interview, the common problems in managing a clinic
   include the difficulties of arranging an appointment with patients,
   keeping the prescription data, and managing payments. Based on these
   problems, in this study, a Clinic Management System (CMAS) mobile
   application was developed using Agile methodology with Mobile-D
   approach. The CMAS app was designed to be easy to use in clinics with
   limited resources when compared to hospitals. The application has admin
   (clinic staff) and patient privileges. The patients can log in,
   register, make a clinic appointment, view prescriptions, and make a
   cashless payment using the Stripe payment gateway. The admin can manage
   and accept the appointments, manage medical prescriptions, and verify
   payments, including viewing invoices. A user acceptance test (UAT) was
   conducted to test the application, which was filled out by nurses,
   doctors, and some patients in the clinic. An overall score of 82.7 out
   of 100 was obtained from the UAT.},
